From 23d8eef109f58fb2edf5f913efe5aca85eb72b9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:26:25 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui, agent_tasks_panel: Open Thread at This Task only
 for a background subagent
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.47 (ask 71, 2026-11-16). The tasks card and the
Agent Tasks panel drew "Open Thread at This Task" on every row. For a
subagent it opens the child thread; for anything else -- a shell or other
task of the main agent -- it only scrolled the same thread to the tool
call, which is not another thread to open. One rule,
tasks_card::offers_open_at_task, now decides it on both surfaces: a
subagent, running in the background, with a child thread or output. The
card makes the button's focus handle only with the button, so Tab never
stops on a missing one; the group header's open is unchanged.

Tests: the rule as a pure function (open_at_task_rule_tests.rs); the card's
accessibility test now uses a background subagent and asserts a shell row
has no Open; the panel's card-buttons test likewise. Two layout tests that
used Open as the first control on a shell row use the eye instead. Red
seen with the rule made always true.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
